cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MASkills in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "MASkills: Continual Skills Optimization for Multi-Agent LLM Systems"
abstract: >-
  Multi-agent LLM systems accumulate task knowledge in a single monolithic
  prompt, where every update overwrites unrelated competence and no individual
  piece of knowledge can be credited, revised, or retired on its own. MASkills
  represents that knowledge as a discrete, persistent skill library and evolves
  it with four typed operators - induct, refine, consolidate, prune - under
  per-skill credit assignment and a held-out validation gate that rolls back a
  candidate library that does not hold up.
type: software
license: MIT
